docs {
  ## Method, Endpoint, and Auth
  
  `GET /api/v1/groups/:groupID` — Active group member or site admin; Bearer access token required.
  
  ## Description
  
  Returns group details and active members with their roles and avatar information (`avatar_attachment_id` and `avatar_url`). Group `status` is `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, or `CLOSED`. The response includes `archived_at` or `closed_at` when the corresponding timestamp is set.
  
  ## Request
  
  ### Path Parameters
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `groupID` | `integer` | Yes | Positive group ID. |
  
  ### Headers
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | `Bearer <access-token>` |
  
  ## Response
  
  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 42,
      "title": "Weekend trip",
      "created_by_user_id": 7,
      "status": "CLOSED",
      "is_premium": false,
      "archived_at": "2026-11-05T10:00:00Z",
      "closed_at": "2026-11-06T10:00:00Z",
      "created_at": "2026-11-04T10:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-06T10:00:00Z",
      "member_count": 2,
      "members": [
        {
          "member_id": 11,
          "user_id": 7,
          "name": "Owner",
          "role": "OWNER",
          "joined_at": "2026-11-04T10:00:00Z",
          "avatar_attachment_id": 101,
          "avatar_url": "https://storage.example.com/attachments/profile_image/7/avatar.jpg?token=..."
        },
        {
          "member_id": 12,
          "user_id": 8,
          "name": "Member",
          "role": "MEMBER",
          "joined_at": "2026-11-04T10:10:00Z",
          "avatar_attachment_id": null,
          "avatar_url": null
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Errors
  
  - `400 GROUP_INVALID_ID` — `groupID` is not a positive integer.
  - `401 MISSING_TOKEN` — Access token is missing or invalid.
  - `403 GROUP_FORBIDDEN` — Requester is neither an active member nor an admin.
  - `404 GROUP_NOT_FOUND` — Group does not exist or was deleted.
  - `500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` — Group details could not be retrieved.
}
